    "body": "## Summary\n\nPins every GitHub Actions `uses:` reference in the CI and coverage workflows to a full commit SHA, while leaving the upstream tag or channel as an inline comment for readability.\n\nFixes marmot-protocol/marmot-security#84.\n\n## Why\n\nThe workflows were using mutable action refs such as `@v4`, `@stable`, `@cargo-audit`, and `@v6`. If an action tag or maintainer account were compromised, future workflow runs could execute changed code without a repository diff.\n\n## Latest refs checked\n\nVerified against upstream GitHub refs on 2026-05-07:\n\n- `actions/checkout`: `v6`\n- `actions/cache`: `v5`\n- `actions/upload-artifact`: `v7`\n- `actions/github-script`: `v9`\n- `dawidd6/action-download-artifact`: `v21`\n- `dtolnay/rust-toolchain`: `stable`\n- `taiki-e/install-action`: `cargo-audit`, `cargo-llvm-cov`\n\n## Validation\n\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/ci.yml .github/workflows/coverage.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |path| YAML.load_file(path); puts \"#{path}: ok\" }' .github/workflows/ci.yml .github/workflows/coverage.yml`\n- `perl -ne 'if (/uses:\\s*\\S+@([^\\s#]+)/ && $1 !~ /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/) { print \"$ARGV:$.:$1\\n\"; $bad=1 } END { exit($bad ? 1 : 0) }' .github/workflows/ci.yml .github/workflows/coverage.yml`\n- Upstream ref comparison for each pinned action SHA\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just ci`\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Chores**\n  * CI workflows updated to pin third‑party GitHub Actions to fixed commit SHAs across verification, test, audit and coverage jobs for improved reproducibility and security. No runtime behavior, job logic, or generated artifacts were changed.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
